<Item XName="GlobalEqns" Attrib="14" Type="Equation">
<Text>FREQ=1e6;&#x000D;&#x000A;TIME=0.0;&#x000D;&#x000A;TEMPERATURE=16.85;&#x000D;&#x000A;Start_Time=0;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Start_Time, &apos;s&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Stop_Time=1;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Stop_Time, &apos;s&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Time_Spacing=.001;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Time_Spacing, &apos;s&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Num_Samples=1001;&#x000D;&#x000A;Sample_Rate=1000;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Sample_Rate, &apos;Hz&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Freq_Resolution=1;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Freq_Resolution, &apos;Hz&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Data_Persistence=0;&#x000D;&#x000A;Start_Time_SC=0;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Start_Time_SC, &apos;s&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Stop_Time_SC=1;&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(Stop_Time_SC, &apos;s&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;Num_Samples_SC=1001;&#x000D;&#x000A;</Text>
<Item XName="BPMgr" Type="BPMgr">
<BPLines><T>Empty</T></BPLines>
<BPStates><T>Empty</T></BPStates></Item>
<Item XName="EqnBlock" Type="EqnBlock">
<Lang><T>Int</T><D>1</D></Lang></Item>
<Item XName="Font" Type="Font">
<Name>Courier New</Name>
<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item>
<Item XName="FunctionBlock" Type="FunctionBlock" />
<Item XName="VarBlock" Type="VarBlock" /></Item>
<Item XName="Note1" UserName="Note1" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;RF_LINK Phased Array : TX vs. RX case studies&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This workspace demonstrates how to apply the results of a Phased Array analysis at the Dataflow level, using RF_LINK.&amp;nbsp; Since the TX case and the RX case are slightlly different, be sure to read the notes on the schematic of the RX dataflow schematic.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;In each case, you need to right-click on the &quot;PlotPattern&quot; equations and select &quot;Run Equations&quot; to create or refresh the 3D plots.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Contents of this workspace&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;Folder &quot;&lt;U&gt;1 Phased&amp;nbsp;Array Tx&lt;/U&gt;&quot;&amp;nbsp; - contains a Phased Array Analysis of a&amp;nbsp;Tx RF Beamforming design &quot;PhasedArrayTxSch&quot;. You can use &quot;PlotPattern1&quot; to run the analysis and plot the directivity pattern.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;Folder &quot;&lt;U&gt;2 RFLink Tx&lt;/U&gt;&quot;&amp;nbsp; - contains a&amp;nbsp;data flow RFLink&amp;nbsp;design using the&amp;nbsp;&quot;PhasedArrayTxSch&quot; schematic (you can drag and drop a RF phased array design to a data flow schematic). You can use &quot;PlotPattern2&quot; to run the analysis and plot the directivity pattern.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;You can compare the directivity patterns computed between Phased Array Analysis and Data Flow Analysis using Phased Array RFLink. The patterns should be the same.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;You can also adjust the input power &quot;Pin&quot; for Tx designs and examine the data flow spectrum&amp;nbsp;to verify that the signal power in data flow should match the phased array analysis including amplifier nonlinearity.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;Folder &quot;&lt;U&gt;3 Phased&amp;nbsp;Array Rx&lt;/U&gt;&quot; contains a Phased Array Analysis of a&amp;nbsp;Rx RF Beamforming design &quot;PhasedArrayRxSch&quot;. You can use &quot;PlotPattern3&quot; to run the analysis and plot the directivity pattern. &lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;Folder &quot;&lt;U&gt;4 RFLink Rx&lt;/U&gt;&quot; contains a&amp;nbsp;data flow RFLink&amp;nbsp;design using the&amp;nbsp;&quot;PhasedArrayRxSch&quot; schematic (you can drag and drop a RF phased array design to a data flow schematic). You can use &quot;PlotPattern4&quot; to run the analysis and plot the directivity pattern.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;</Text>
