<Item XName="SetupTx" UserName="SetupTx" Type="Equation">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>% The input power will be chosen to be at the 1 dB compression point of the&#x000D;&#x000A;% RF amplifier. Since OP1dB = +10 dBm then IP1dB will be at -9 dBm. At the&#x000D;&#x000A;% input to the phase shifter this will be -8 dBm. Since the splitter is 64&#x000D;&#x000A;% way the split loss is 18.062 dB and including the insertion loss we have a&#x000D;&#x000A;% total split loss of 19.062 dB therefore the P1dB at the input to the splitter&#x000D;&#x000A;% is +11.062 dBm&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;Pin = 11.062; %dBm&#x000D;&#x000A;Fin = 1000; %MHz&#x000D;&#x000A;</Text>
